cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its findings, please cite it."
title: "AI Name-Pronunciation Fairness Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible benchmark measuring how accurately text-to-speech
  systems pronounce personal names from African languages (Yoruba, Igbo, Hausa)
  compared to common English names, using ASR back-transcription and an
  ASR-independent phoneme layer, with statistical significance testing.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amhanesi
    given-names: Peace
repository-code: "https://github.com/amhanesipeace/name-pronunciation-benchmark"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
keywords:
  - text-to-speech
  - speech synthesis
  - fairness
  - bias
  - responsible AI
  - African languages
  - Yoruba
  - Igbo
  - Hausa
  - name pronunciation
